# These should point at the Neon "development" branch, never at production
# (see docs/adr/0014-separate-dev-test-database-branch.md). Production's
# values live in Vercel's Production environment settings (the only place
# the live app reads them from) and, for the one-off `migrate:production`
# script only (see docs/requirements/infrastructure-deployment/11-production-deployment-pipeline.md
# and docs/adr/0019-local-production-credentials-and-automated-migrations.md),
# in a separate, gitignored .env.migrate-production.local -- never in this
# file. Deliberately NOT named .env.production.local: Next.js auto-loads
# that exact filename during any local `next build`/`next start`, which
# would silently point a local run at production.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require"
# Non-pooled connection, used only by Prisma Migrate (see docs/adr/0003-postgres-database-via-neon.md)
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require"

# Used only to classify an ingredient's grocery category when it's first
# added (see docs/requirements/printing-exports/12-menu-print-preview.md and the AI-service
# ADR it calls for). Not a database credential -- a different kind of
# secret this app didn't need before. If unset or invalid, classification
# silently falls back to a built-in keyword heuristic rather than failing.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="sk-ant-..."

# Used only as transient transport for the PDF/Excel campout-import upload
# (see docs/requirements/data-import/30-campout-import-from-pdf-excel.md and
# docs/adr/0032-campout-import-blob-upload-transport.md) -- the file is
# uploaded straight from the browser to Vercel Blob and deleted again right
# after the server reads it, never kept as persistent storage. Get this by
# creating a Blob store in the Vercel dashboard (Storage tab) for this
# project -- set its access to **Private** (can't be changed after
# creation; public would make the uploaded file briefly fetchable by
# anyone with the URL, no auth at all) and connect it to Production,
# Preview, AND Development (Development isn't preselected). That
# auto-adds this var to Vercel's own connected environments, but local
# dev still needs it pulled down by hand (`vercel env pull
# .env.development.local`, or copy it from the dashboard) for the import
# feature to work in local dev. Without it, uploads fail with a clear
# "Invalid upload" error rather than a silent crash. One store is shared
# across all environments here (unlike DATABASE_URL above) -- this blob
# never holds persistent data, so there's nothing for a shared store to
# put at risk the way a shared database would.
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN="vercel_blob_rw_..."

# REQ-31/ADR 0033: signs and encrypts Better Auth's session cookies and
# tokens -- this app's auth library, replacing ADR 0010's cookie-only
# identity. Generate with `openssl rand -base64 32` (or equivalent); treat
# it like any other credential -- rotating it invalidates every existing
# session, so there's no "lost it, no big deal" recovery, just a forced
# re-login for everyone.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET="replace-with-a-real-random-32-byte-value"

# REQ-31.3/ADR 0033: sends the magic-link bootstrap/recovery email -- this
# app's first email-sending need. Get an API key at resend.com. If unset,
# lib/email.ts logs the link to the console instead of sending it, so local
# dev works without a real Resend account (same "missing external secret
# degrades gracefully" pattern as ANTHROPIC_API_KEY above).
RESEND_API_KEY="re_..."
# Must be a domain verified in the Resend dashboard for real delivery;
# Resend's own sandbox address (the default in lib/email.ts) only delivers
# to the account's own verified email, fine for initial testing only.
RESEND_FROM_ADDRESS="ScoutBuddy <onboarding@resend.dev>"
